# Database local rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/engineering/database.md` first.
- Identify every touched table as Workbench-owned or existing ZenTao before
  applying model, audit, or soft-delete conventions.
- Parameterize values; select only required columns. Never interpolate dynamic
  values into SQL. Closed server-controlled structural fragments are allowed
  under database.md; trace their builders and keep user values in placeholders.
- List queries normally perform filter, sort, count, and pagination in SQL.
- Reject unbounded load-then-page, looped per-row SQL, repeated same-request
  dictionary loads, and unevaluated metric query fan-out.
- Keep business and authorization decisions in Service even when SQL helps derive
  facts. Follow architecture.md for transaction ownership and cross-Repo approval.
- Follow database.md for shared-writer lock order, state rechecks, idempotency,
  batch/time budgets, read-after-write consistency and isolated concurrency tests.
- A stored config is not DB access authorization; evidence must match the target.
- Committed configuration contains placeholders only; secrets enter at runtime.
